.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW-IP-RULES" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-ip-rules - Show or set which client addresses may open this preview


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview ip-rules <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Without flags, show the preview's IP allow and deny lists. --allow and --deny take an address or CIDR and repeat; each replaces that whole list. An address a deny entry matches is refused, and when the allow list is not empty only its addresses get in. Refused visitors see 403 "Access to this link is restricted".

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--allow\fP=[]
	address or CIDR allowed in (repeatable; replaces the allow list)

.PP
\fB--clear\fP[=false]
	remove both lists

.PP
\fB--deny\fP=[]
	address or CIDR refused (repeatable; replaces the deny list)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ip-rules

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the lists as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
